      "biography": {
        "value": "<h2>Description</h2><p>This land-bound predator has the head of a bird of prey and four legs with wickedly sharp, sickle-like talons on their feet, but between the rat-like tail, its stubby wings that can't be used to fly, and its general downcast expression, it just comes off as sad…- Imban</p><h2>Defense</h2><p>AC 16, touch 11, flat-footed 14 (+2 Dex, +5 natural, -1 size)</p><p>hp 30 [48] (4d10+8)</p><p>Fort +6, Ref +6, Will +4</p><h2>Offense</h2><p>Speed 30 ft.</p><p>Melee bite +6 (1d8+3), 2 talons +6 (1d8+3)</p><p>Space 10 ft.; Reach 5 ft.</p><p>Special Attacks pounce, rake (2 talons +6, 1d8+3)</p><h2>Statistics</h2><p>Str 16, Dex 15, Con 14, Int 6, Wis 13, Cha 6</p><p>Base Atk +4; CMB +8; CMD 19 (23 vs. trip)</p><p>Feats Improved Natural Attack (Talon), Iron Will</p><p>Skills Acrobatics +11, Perception +10; Racial Modifiers +4 Acrobatics, +4 Perception</p><h2>Ecology</h2><p>Environment cold mountains, underground</p><p>Organization solitary, pair, or pride (6-10)</p><p>Treasure incidental</p>"
      }
